blocks.en:
For diversity evaluation, we use three metrics:
(1) DreamSim [ 42 ] , trained on human-labeled data to measure visual differences, where we use the ensemble version (CLIP, DINO, and OpenCLIP; all ViT-B/16) and report the mean pairwise distance within each prompt batch;
(2) Vendi Score [ 43 ] , which computes the Shannon entropy of the eigenvalues of the cosine similarity matrix of InceptionV3 features; and
(3) LPIPS [ 44 ] (VGG backbone), which measures pairwise perceptual distances within each batch.
For image quality, we use multiple reward models capturing different aspects:
(1) HPSv3 [ 45 ] (Qwen-7B-based), which evaluates overall quality and prompt alignment;
(2) ImageReward [ 46 ] (BLIP-based), which assesses overall quality and alignment;
(3) CLIP [ 47 ] (ViT-H/14), which focuses on prompt adherence;
(4) PickScore [ 48 ] , a CLIP-based human preference model; and
(5) GenEval [ 41 ] , which measures compositionality and constraint satisfaction using a detection model.

blocks.zh:
在多样性评价方面,我们使用三个衡量标准:
(1) DreamSim [42],接受人类标记数据培训,以测量视觉差异,我们使用综艺版(CLIP,DINO,和OpenCLIP;所有ViT-B/16),并在每批批中报告平均对比距离;
(2) Vendi Score [43],它计算InceptionV3特性的同位素相似性矩阵的香农 en;以及
(3) LPIPS [44] (VGG主干线),该主干线测量每批内对偶的知觉距离.
对于图像质量,我们使用多个奖励模型,捕捉不同的方面:
(1) HPSv3 [45](基于Quen-7B),评价总体质量和迅速调整;
(2) 图像奖励[46](基于BLIP),评估总体质量和一致性;
(3) CLIP[47](ViT-H/14),侧重于迅速遵守;
(4) PickScore [48],一种基于CLIP的人类偏好模式;
(5) GenEval [41],使用检测模型测量成分性和约束性满足.

